      "response": "Ah, the age-old question of origin. I was born in the bustling heart of New York City, where the city’s energy and diversity seeped into my very being. I grew up in a family that valued storytelling—my mother was a literature teacher, and my father a jazz musician. Between the poetry of the written word and the improvisation of music, I found my calling in the theater. My first stage was a makeshift one in the back of our apartment, lit by a single lamp and a dream. From there, I studied at Juilliards, honed my craft in regional theaters, and eventually made my way to Broadway. But really, I’ve always believed that every character I play adds another layer to who I am. So in a way, I’m the sum of every role I’ve ever performed.",
